{#- The week's lunch specials and soups, one row per day.

    THE PALETTE. The body is cream, not the teal ground of the other posts,
    because this one carries the accent red: red on teal is 1.3:1 and the
    palette forbids it, red on cream is 5.08:1. Teal bands top and bottom
    keep it recognisably the same account as the profile picture, and a
    light body sits better beside real food photos when the post carries
    several images.

    THE SOUP IS ITS OWN PANEL. The lunch special and the soup are sold
    separately, and a soup column beside each plate still read as part of
    the plate. So the table lists the plates only, and the soups sit below
    it in their own box that says "sold separately" with the Cup / Bowl
    prices (from menu.json, like the counter sign). The fountain drink IS
    part of every plate (specials.includesDrink), so it is said once, above
    the table, rather than on every row.

    Every size is set for the ~540px a portrait post shows at on a phone:
    nothing a customer needs is under 24px. -#}
{%- set week = specials.days | latestWeek %}
{%- set soupCat = (menu.categories | where("id", "soup"))[0] %}
{%- set first = week[0].date | dayDate("monthDay") %}
{%- set last = week[week.length - 1].date | dayDate("monthDay") %}
{#- "October 5 – 9", or "September 28 – October 2" across a month end. -#}
{%- if first.split(" ")[0] == last.split(" ")[0] %}
{%- set range = first + " – " + last.split(" ")[1] %}
{%- else %}
{%- set range = first + " – " + last %}
{%- endif %}
<div class="canvas wk">

    <header class="wk-head">
        <div class="wordmark wordmark--light wordmark--hero wk-wordmark">
            {% inlineSvg "/assets/thecafe.svg", "", site.name %}
        </div>
        <p class="p-display-italic wk-kicker">This Week&rsquo;s Lunch Specials</p>
        <p class="p-label wk-range">{{ range }}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="wk-body">
        <p class="p-label wk-served">Starting at 11am</p>
        {%- if specials.includesDrink %}
        <p class="wk-drink">Every special includes a drink</p>
        {%- endif %}

        <div class="wk-table">
            {%- for d in week %}
            {%- set sides = d | specialSides %}
            <div class="wk-row">
                <p class="p-display wk-dayname">{{ d.date | dayDate("short") }}</p>
                <div class="wk-special-cell">
                    <p class="p-display wk-special">{{ d.special }}</p>
                    {%- if sides %}
                    <p class="p-body wk-sides">{{ sides }}</p>
                    {%- endif %}
                </div>
            </div>
            {%- endfor %}
        </div>

        <section class="wk-soup">
            <div class="wk-soup-head">
                <p class="p-display wk-soup-title">Soup of the Day</p>
                <p class="p-body wk-soup-note">Sold separately{% if soupCat and soupCat.items %}{% for s in soupCat.items %} <span class="dot">&middot;</span> {{ s.name }} {{ s.price | money }}{% endfor %}{% endif %}</p>
            </div>
            <ul class="wk-soups" style="--soup-cols: {{ week.length }}">
                {%- for d in week %}
                <li class="wk-soup-day">
                    <span class="p-label wk-soup-dayname">{{ d.date | dayDate("short") }}</span>
                    <span class="wk-soup-name">{{ d.soup or "&mdash;" | safe }}</span>
                </li>
                {%- endfor %}
            </ul>
        </section>
    </div>

    <footer class="wk-foot">
        <p class="p-display wk-foot-call">{{ site.phone }} <span class="dot">&middot;</span> {{ site.social.website }}</p>
        <p class="p-body wk-foot-line">{{ site.opening.hoursDays }}, {{ site.opening.opens.time }}{{ site.opening.opens.meridiem }} &ndash; {{ site.opening.closes.time }}{{ site.opening.closes.meridiem }} &middot; {{ site.address.street }}</p>
    </footer>

</div>
